{
  "$note": "The DS now ships 32 CAPTURED chart configurations across 9 categories — the product's own chart-builder output, sanitised. They are shipped in this spec package under `charts/` (config JSON per fixture) with an index at `charts/manifest.json`, and are shown live at the showcase `…/elements/charts.html` (overview + a page per category). HOW TO USE: pick the category below, take the matching fixture's `config` and render it with Highcharts v10 — `Highcharts.chart(el, config)` (the custom-engine ones — gauge, heat-map, anomaly, forecast, some map/top-n — carry a `result` payload instead, drawn by a small custom renderer, not Highcharts). KNOWN GAPS (captured, not guessed): (1) formatter FUNCTIONS cannot be serialised — a \"«fn»\" marker means the product had a formatter there, so tooltips/axis labels fall back to engine defaults; (2) fixtures were captured in the product's DARK theme — a light-theme capture is still pending. Colour series from the categorical palette / severity tokens, never the brand navy --primary.",
  "engine": "Highcharts v10 (+ highcharts-more, solid-gauge, sankey, heatmap, treemap, map, no-data-to-display); Leaflet for the online map",
